<title>HUNGARY: Hungarian farmers to block roads from Monday.</title>
<headline>Hungarian farmers to block roads from Monday.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian farmers decided on Wednesday to begin a three-day blockade from Monday of main roads to protest at new tax regulations, following the breakdown of last ditch talks with government officials.</p>
<p>The farmers presented a petition last week to the agricultural ministry giving the cabinet until Tuesday evening to withdraw tax and social security measures introduced on January 1 which they say jeopardise their livelihood.</p>
<p>&quot;The deadline has passed with no response to our demands,&quot; protest committee chairman Gyula Kosa told Hungarian television. &quot;What happens now is the government's responsibility not ours.&quot;</p>
<p>The farmers said they will set up over 25 road blocks outside key towns around Hungary, a move which will almost certainly paralyse the country's road system.</p>
</text>
